@startuml
title Owner decision — Like — v4

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor Owner
boundary "Browser SPA" as Browser
control "FERTO Worker" as Worker
participant "Spotify Web API" as Spotify
database "D1" as D1

Owner -> Browser: Click "Like" on the current recommendation
Browser -> Worker: POST /api/owner/like { trackId }\nOrigin + X-CSRF-Token + owner session cookie

alt Visitor, wrong origin, missing CSRF,\nnot the configured owner, or invalid track id
  Worker --> Browser: 401 / 403 / 400 — before any Spotify call
else Valid owner request
  Worker -> Spotify: Grant SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN\n(service token, includes user-library-modify)
  Spotify --> Worker: Access token

  Worker -> D1: Resolve canonical + exact live/staging aliases\nin one generation snapshot
  alt Resolved identity is still exact-id only
    Worker -> Spotify: GET /v1/tracks/{oldId} to confirm ISRC
    alt Transient metadata failure
      Worker --> Browser: 503 — candidate retained; Spotify save not attempted
    end
  end

  Worker -> Spotify: PUT /v1/me/library?uris=spotify:track:{trackId}\n— **saved to Spotify first**

  alt Spotify save fails
    Spotify --> Worker: Non-success response
    Worker --> Browser: 502 — the candidate is retained
    Browser --> Owner: "Could not save — the track stays"
    note right of Worker #FFDDDD
      Failure retention: nothing is excluded
      locally when Spotify did not confirm the
      save, so the recording is not lost from
      both the library and the shelf at once.
    end note
  else Spotify save confirmed
    Spotify --> Worker: Success
    Worker -> D1: Re-read live + active destinations in one snapshot\n(either side of a concurrent promotion)
    Worker -> D1: INSERT OR IGNORE the recording key into\nrebuild_known_recordings for the live generation\nAND every active staging generation
    Worker -> D1: Atomic serialized batch: remove its live track slot\nand compact the track/artist slot ranges + counters
    note right of D1
      The exclusion is recording-wide under every
      alias: another representative of the same
      ISRC is hidden too, and a staging
      generation promoted later stays excluded.
    end note
    Worker --> Browser: 200 { ok: true }
    Browser -> Worker: GET /api/recommendation (next track)
    Worker --> Browser: A different recommendation, if one is available
  end
end

@enduml
